---
globs:
  - "src/settings/featureModes.ts"
  - "src/settings/envKeys.ts"
  - "src/settings/config.ts"
  - "src/settings/slices/features.ts"
  - "src/agentWork/intake/**"
  - "src/webhook/**"
  - ".env.example"
  - "docs/features.md"
  - "test/settingsInventory.test.ts"
  - "test/featureConfig.test.ts"
---
The nine `FEATURE_*` keys in `ENV` (`src/settings/envKeys.ts`) are the only user-facing capability switches, including `FEATURE_REVIEW_CADENCE`. Allowed modes live in `src/settings/featureModes.ts`: `REVIEW_FEATURE_MODES` has no `off`, `COMMAND_FEATURE_MODES` (ask, triage) has no `auto`, and `FEATURE_COMMIT_STATUS` / `FEATURE_TITLE_REWRITE` are strict booleans. `loadConfig` reads them with `readEnum` / `readStrictBoolean`, which throw `config.invalid_enum`. Auto triggers are fixed in `planAutomatedPullRequestIntake` (`src/agentWork/intake/delivery.ts`); do not add env knobs for them. Approval mode decides author trust on open and consumes awaiting state once through `reviewApprovals.ts`; approving deliveries cannot infer permission from an active-work precheck. A new feature or mode changes `Features`, `featureModes.ts`, `ENV`, `config.ts`, `.env.example`, and `docs/features.md` in one PR; `test/settingsInventory.test.ts` pins 9 `FEATURE_*` keys and 72 `ENV` keys.
